1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Hello! We are Team Azoic from Dhaka, Bangladesh.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:11,500
We are competing in NASA Space Apps 2026 for the challenge: Field Shift: Adapting Farms with NASA Data.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:17,000
Meet Abdul, a smallholder farmer cultivating 1.0 hectare in Godagari, Rajshahi.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000
For generations, Abdul has followed a rigid Boro-Fallow-Aman rotation.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,500
He pumps groundwater for winter rice, leaves soil bare for 75 days in pre-monsoon heat,

6
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,000
and relies on erratic monsoon rains for Aman.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,500
Step 2: Why single-season weather forecasts are not enough.

8
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:43,000
Climate change is shifting the monsoon onset across Bangladesh.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Rather than guessing, FieldShift grounds every recommendation in 25 years of NASA Earth observations:

10
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,000
NASA POWER climatology, high-resolution NASA GPM IMERG precipitation, and SoilGrids.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,500
And we maintain absolute honesty: our IMERG cross-validation shows no false onset claims.

12
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:06,000
Step 3: Ground-level physics and aquifer stress.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,500
NASA GRACE-FO gravitational satellite telemetry confirms that the Barind aquifer is declining at -1.07 cm/year.

14
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:18,500
Deep tubewell diesel costs are soaring, and pumping more water is unsustainable.

15
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:25,000
Abdul cannot just change planting dates; he must adapt his entire multi-season rotation.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Step 4: The multi-season optimization engine.

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:36,500
FieldShift solves a multi-period mathematical model across 6 consecutive planning seasons.

18
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:43,000
It evaluates cash budgets, water pumping limits, and crop-specific soil texture suitability matrices.

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
In Rajshahi, the Water-Saving strategy replaces high-water Boro with low-water Mustard and Mungbean.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,500
Step 5: Transparent, plain-language answers.

21
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:01,000
Anyone—a farmer, an extension officer, or a judge—understands the result in 3 seconds.

22
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The answer header states: You save ~809 mm irrigation water, add 35 kg soil nitrogen,

23
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,500
and gain an estimated +155,000 BDT extra profit.

24
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:18,000
Step 6: The ultimate proof: Two-Field Regional Divergence.

25
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:24,500
Watch how FieldShift's recommendation flips between regions!

26
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:30,500
In drought-prone Rajshahi, GRACE depletion and clay terrace force low-water Mustard.

27
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:36,500
In Sunamganj haor basin, 3-meter monsoon floods make Kharif farming impossible;

28
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:43,000
receding winter beels provide 1,104 mm surface water, making single-season Boro rice viable with 49,200 BDT margin.

29
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:49,500
One algorithm, two completely different regional realities—pure physics, zero hardcoding.

30
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:55,000
In our 3D Farm Diorama, crop plans come to life.

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Using lightweight Three.js InstancedMesh with less than 60 draw calls, crop rows reflect the exact strategy:

32
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:09,500
water sheets over Aman paddy, yellow flowering mustard in winter, and bare tilled furrows during fallow.

33
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:15,000
On the Water page, our Soil-Water Column visualizes FAO-56 root-zone depletion in real-time,

34
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:22,000
showing rainfall drops, evapotranspiration vapour, and AWD thresholds to save 25% to 30% fuel.

35
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,500
FieldShift reaches every farmer: through modern web dashboards, high-contrast daylight mode,

36
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:34,500
printable A4 cards, and plain-text SMS for basic feature phones.

37
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:41,000
Most importantly, it operates 100% offline with zero external dependencies.

38
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:48,000
FieldShift equips farmers with 25 years of NASA Earth observation science to adapt, conserve water, and prosper.

39
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:54,000
We are Team Azoic, and this is FieldShift 2026.

40
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Thank you!
